      "math_academy_id": "q-102613",
      "sequence_position": 47,
      "problem": "Find the instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)=10{x}^{2}$ at the point $x=3$ by computing the limit of a difference quotient.",
      "worked_solution": "*Method 1:*\n\nBy the definition, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(3)={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(3+h)-f(3)}{h}.\n$$\n\nApplying this to $f(x)=10{x}^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{10(3+h)^{2}-10(3)^{2}}{h}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{90+60h+10{h}^{2}-90}{h}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{60h+10{h}^{2}}{h}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(60+10h) \\\\  & =60+(0) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Method 2:*\n\nBy the definition, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(3)={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{f(x)-f(3)}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nApplying this to $f(x)=10{x}^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\frac{10{x}^{2}-10(3)^{2}}{x-3}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\frac{10({x}^{2}-{3}^{2})}{x-3}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\frac{10(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}10(x+3) \\\\  & =10(3+3) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
